WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Canada is the second-largest country in the world by land area, renowned for pristine lakes and boreal forests.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Mount Logan in the Yukon Saint Elias Mountains reaches 5,959 meters as Canada's highest peak.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
English and French are the two official languages, with French centered in the province of Quebec.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Indigenous First Nations and Inuit cultures preserve intricate soapstone carvings and totem poles.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Iconic Canadian cuisine features pure maple syrup tapped from sugar maples and Montreal poutine.

